joshua_russo: Must be divine punishment for you. [pause=0.5]Or maybe a divine reward on my end.[pause=0.5] Probably not that, given my love of things that would have me burned at the stake years ago.
joshua_russo: How lucky am I? [pause=0.5]Seriously, this is incredible.
He holds up the old tome.
joshua_russo: The book has a history, but bringing its current owner back from the dead? [pause=0.5]Haha…I never would’ve guessed, I’ll have to look into that when I get back.
player: Russo…[pause=0.5] you…
joshua_russo: Call me Josh, surely we’re close enough now to drop the formalities.
player: You–[pause=0.5]you killed me!
joshua_russo: Yeah. I did. [pause=0.5]Felt pretty bad about it at first, you know? [pause=0.5]I just wanted all the shit you stole from my house back. [pause=0.5]I could’ve forgiven the book, honestly. But you made a mistake with that locket. [pause=0.5]You put your hands on {playerName}. [pause=0.5]And I could never forgive that.
player: ...{playerName}?
joshua_russo: Oh. [pause=0.5]Yeah, sorry. [pause=0.5]That’s whose soul is currently in the locket you stole. [pause=0.5]As much as it pissed me off to hear you speak that name, I got a kick out of you not remembering your own.[pause=0.5] It was so damn hard to track you down with all the bullshit I had to wade through. [pause=0.5]You’re a parasite, you take and take. [pause=0.5]You had no value to society, so it was easy enough for you to swap names on the fly I guess. [pause=0.5]Me, I’m more of a giftgiver. [pause=0.5]When I gave this to {playerName} on our anniversary, I still remember that look in their eyes…[pause=0.5]one you’ve probably never seen in anyone else’s.
player: ......
joshua_russo: {playerName} is back with me, and that’s all I really needed. [pause=0.5]Not sure what’ll happen when I take the book out of here, but frankly, I don’t care.[pause=0.5] If you try and haunt me, I’ll just use it to make your death even worse than your life. [pause=0.5]How’s that sound?
player: I’m sorry.[pause=0.5] I’m sorry. [pause=0.5]I’m sorry. [pause=0.5]Please. [pause=0.5]Please.[pause=0.5] Don’t leave me like this.[pause=0.5] I messed up. [pause=0.5]I know. [pause=0.5]That book brought me back, right!? [pause=0.5]What else can it do!?
joshua_russo: None of my concern. [pause=0.5]Have a good afterlife, Harper.